    {
     "line": 663,
     "heading": "### Rule 101: Verification - a recorded fingerprint is refreshed after the last edit to what it covers, and the final snapshot re-runs its checker",
     "chars": 1009,
     "sha256": "e8dd0502a2e3c4187ddab0bf6fe711fbf898192d95f6df4b1df890d6075622d1",
     "dest": "skills/_engineering/rules/verification.md"
    },
    {
     "line": 669,
     "heading": "### Rule 102: Optional SDKs - check request arguments against the installed client at construction, and test the oldest and newest SDK",
     "chars": 876,
     "sha256": "8820fc7b95fa1842256fdc777ced54ff5cef09ef5405766bbdd68e102e784857",
     "dest": "skills/_engineering/rules/packaging.md"
    },
    {
     "line": 675,
     "heading": "### Rule 103: Responses - read the status before the payload",
     "chars": 719,
     "sha256": "de9131e00663549cd24b5ae23e0b020daef10e5796402ccf508c29823daa323a",
     "dest": "skills/_engineering/rules/contracts.md"
    },
    {
     "line": 681,
     "heading": "### Rule 104: Untrusted structured output - store only the validated schema",
     "chars": 689,
     "sha256": "6392bccd386179e41c898bb04122c2e170e772888acc02a239f525ccfd7f7348",
     "dest": "skills/_engineering/rules/contracts.md"
    },
    {
     "line": 687,
     "heading": "### Rule 105: Caller-supplied resources - classify their failures apart from the remote's, and count from the source",
     "chars": 957,
     "sha256": "bfca26c08ba3e1a1439fb6a713fe3d46fccbe9942ef8dc8c4881a62609969dea",
     "dest": "skills/_engineering/rules/contracts.md"
    },
    {
     "line": 693,
     "heading": "### Rule 106: Loaders - a record is checked against an explicit per-field contract before an object is built from it",
     "chars": 883,
     "sha256": "ba1bee26289222120d2a7e706b5a76c6bb0b7c4b382e1c3960a59d7af92b0559",
     "dest": "skills/_engineering/rules/contracts.md"
    },
    {
     "line": 699,
     "heading": "### Rule 107: Exporters - refuse at write time what the loader cannot read back",
     "chars": 820,
     "sha256": "3173f0c4caa4637411bf8ed8d2bf7e11dae84ecc264f8fcdf9a05193fb7375ec",
     "dest": "skills/_engineering/rules/contracts.md"
    },
    {
     "line": 705,
     "heading": "### Rule 108: Identities - a reader of persisted data refuses another generation by its own error, never by the \"malformed row\" path",
     "chars": 1098,
     "sha256": "cd4adaf6b06ad7dcbc052e6fc6fecbdee78edb4f1569dc24e9b19a7f17eb27d7",
     "dest": "skills/_engineering/rules/contracts.md"
    },
    {
     "line": 711,
     "heading": "### Rule 109: Concurrency - per-process state is fork-safe per instance, not by a module hook",
     "chars": 798,
     "sha256": "158da0cf27dc96b45dad1b60ea7f534ca287d4e40603428e6d88a646d297d0dc",
     "dest": "skills/_engineering/rules/state.md"
    },
    {
     "line": 717,
     "heading": "### Rule 110: Options - a new option is validated on assignment and reaches every producer, wrappers and plans included",
     "chars": 820,
     "sha256": "2dc4af796139c6bcc7f97987aece1e844f8f0bc636b62bae2f03d275c9d4816b",
     "dest": "skills/_engineering/rules/contracts.md"
    },
    {
     "line": 723,
     "heading": "### Rule 111: Identities - text is hashed with `surrogatepass`, never `replace`",
     "chars": 678,
     "sha256": "5c5427f9c486e0a92cee906d57ab124b9542f12a51e65c7a628b03327eba55d4",
     "dest": "skills/_engineering/rules/contracts.md"
    },
    {
     "line": 729,
     "heading": "### Rule 112: Contracts - a shared value object is hashable, picklable and copyable, and a contract runs inside each caller's resilience boundary",
     "chars": 915,
     "sha256": "16419c00d111385871a8fa7c5bb5a3cd4089d715978dbdea5d55df817559f8f3",
     "dest": "skills/_engineering/rules/contracts.md"
    },
    {
     "line": 735,
     "heading": "### Rule 113: Exactness - sort on floats, decide near ties exactly",
     "chars": 744,
     "sha256": "82dd85d6b5359cfbf73ff80710ad4daa7b54661a1cd8a33d2aaa367dc04897ce",
     "dest": "skills/_engineering/rules/numerics.md"
    },
    {
     "line": 741,
     "heading": "### Rule 114: Scope - a scope applies at every read seam and to every statistic that ranks",
     "chars": 1292,
     "sha256": "b03ae612093d3531052fd783c631d1aa60fa0b5b156c529396e396c66f6af883",
     "dest": "skills/_engineering/rules/contracts.md"
    },
    {
     "line": 747,
     "heading": "### Rule 115: Fallbacks - a refusal has its own error type, and \"broken\" needs evidence",
     "chars": 1255,
     "sha256": "284700ef65538317a72f6b3d13fdec45c1f034d15d7f6573719efced829730ae",
     "dest": "skills/_engineering/rules/contracts.md"
    },
    {
     "line": 753,
     "heading": "### Rule 116: Name tables - one shared instance is the default everywhere, and built-ins never displace a user's entry",
     "chars": 1091,
     "sha256": "88c0aabacbdd3fef3f2ac256767887c39375008694d9998b42164a186b2feab2",
     "dest": "skills/_engineering/rules/contracts.md"
    },
    {
     "line": 759,
     "heading": "### Rule 117: Spans - an unknown or foreign region is reported as unknown, never as the whole parent",
     "chars": 1131,
     "sha256": "7f710ab0e0f40545505ee673210658d6358b5af58250f5d96950c40b845c7409",
     "dest": "skills/_engineering/rules/text.md"
    },
    {
     "line": 765,
     "heading": "### Rule 118: Stores that gain deletion - every reader treats a vanished entry as a miss, and a bound never evicts for an entry it then refuses",
     "chars": 1233,
     "sha256": "ca9f231d29221884b99e5e495261646260a6f0dcb0343702574d7dcb8a6ae0be",
     "dest": "skills/_engineering/rules/state.md"
    },
    {
     "line": 771,
     "heading": "### Rule 119: Optional dependencies - prove each called API exists in a real install, and test with the dependency present",
     "chars": 1249,
     "sha256": "b8e9f7b6132bce12f8f843b74f455693a86d36e4bdcdd8c6f4796ff0148a8dd8",
     "dest": "skills/_engineering/rules/packaging.md"
    },
    {
     "line": 777,
     "heading": "### Rule 120: Waiting on a background process - never match its name with a command whose own text contains it",
     "chars": 1085,
     "sha256": "1e263851efe028bc2a642040860968c683fb51044ec54d5ca2256bf4e149282e",
     "dest": "skills/_engineering/rules/tooling.md"
    },
    {
     "line": 783,
     "heading": "### Rule 121: Tooling - the escape conversion of Rule 52 also happens in shell heredocs, and to visible characters",
     "chars": 1163,
     "sha256": "72f825b97c76f521797387aafa40ca6335bf86ebec589697a8b3a1dad48bed13",
     "dest": "skills/_engineering/rules/tooling.md"
    },
    {
     "line": 789,
     "heading": "### Rule 122: Markup parsers - a parser that claims a reference syntax is tested against the reference implementation",
     "chars": 1221,
     "sha256": "0bc28e9a970be12f8d1ec3c02be6360bf2e5aed3e6dfae2f0d851f1c26105915",
     "dest": "skills/_engineering/rules/text.md"
    },
    {
     "line": 795,
     "heading": "### Rule 123: Gates - a missing base makes every old finding look new",
     "chars": 650,
     "sha256": "62facc8e930776da98aa0ae7775ea6d4477308e5495fc13f6887d2f8e567bf4b",
     "dest": "skills/_engineering/rules/verification.md"
    },
    {
